{"2419010": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "Backrooms: Wit's End", "steam_appid": 2419010, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A unique take on the popular &quot;Backrooms&quot; creepypasta lore, with a focus on dynamic experiences, with <strong>procedural levels</strong>, <strong>non-linear</strong> level progression, complex entities, and engaging puzzles to keep the game fresh and replayable over time.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > <br><i>&quot;If you're not careful and you noclip out of reality in the wrong areas, you'll end up in the Backrooms, where it's nothing but the stink of old moist carpet, the madness of mono-yellow, the endless background noise of fluorescent lights at maximum hum-buzz, and approximately six hundred million square miles of randomly segmented empty rooms to be trapped in.</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>God save you if you hear something wandering around nearby, because it sure as hell has heard you&quot;</i></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Real Backrooms experience: Procedural and non-linear.</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Discover the true unpredictability of the Backrooms: shifting layouts, <strong>procedurally generated</strong> levels, and <strong>non-linear</strong> exploration that capture the chaos and mystery the original lore intended.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>At your Wit's End</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > The deeply unsettling and inexplicable nature of the Backrooms pushes the player's sanity to its limit. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You must keep your sanity in check while playing, staying clear of dark or disturbed areas, and avoiding entities, otherwise, your senses might start failing you. </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Multiplayer</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Enter the Backrooms together with your friends (or find a public lobby!), up to <strong>6 players</strong> per lobby!  and work your way to escape the many different levels, communicating through proximity voice chat with the other players.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Level Progression</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > More than one different exit in each level creates a complex and engaging navigation experience between layers and levels, be sure to not get lost. </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Entities</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Face entities that actually think. Each one follows complex, learnable behaviors and movement patterns, challenging players to observe, adapt, and escape. </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Participate in the game's development!</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game is under active development, expect regular content updates with new levels, entities, and puzzles!  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You can participate directly in the game development by providing your feedback through the game's community page and joining the Discord server!</p>", "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A unique take on the popular &quot;Backrooms&quot; creepypasta lore, with a focus on dynamic experiences, with <strong>procedural levels</strong>, <strong>non-linear</strong> level progression, complex entities, and engaging puzzles to keep the game fresh and replayable over time.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > <br><i>&quot;If you're not careful and you noclip out of reality in the wrong areas, you'll end up in the Backrooms, where it's nothing but the stink of old moist carpet, the madness of mono-yellow, the endless background noise of fluorescent lights at maximum hum-buzz, and approximately six hundred million square miles of randomly segmented empty rooms to be trapped in.</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>God save you if you hear something wandering around nearby, because it sure as hell has heard you&quot;</i></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Real Backrooms experience: Procedural and non-linear.</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Discover the true unpredictability of the Backrooms: shifting layouts, <strong>procedurally generated</strong> levels, and <strong>non-linear</strong> exploration that capture the chaos and mystery the original lore intended.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>At your Wit's End</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > The deeply unsettling and inexplicable nature of the Backrooms pushes the player's sanity to its limit. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You must keep your sanity in check while playing, staying clear of dark or disturbed areas, and avoiding entities, otherwise, your senses might start failing you. </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Multiplayer</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Enter the Backrooms together with your friends (or find a public lobby!), up to <strong>6 players</strong> per lobby!  and work your way to escape the many different levels, communicating through proximity voice chat with the other players.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Level Progression</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > More than one different exit in each level creates a complex and engaging navigation experience between layers and levels, be sure to not get lost. </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Entities</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Face entities that actually think. Each one follows complex, learnable behaviors and movement patterns, challenging players to observe, adapt, and escape. </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Participate in the game's development!</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game is under active development, expect regular content updates with new levels, entities, and puzzles!  </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You can participate directly in the game development by providing your feedback through the game's community page and joining the Discord server!</p>", "short_description": "Backrooms: Wit's End is an immersive coop survival horror game, featuring procedurally generated, non-linear level progression and dynamic gameplay mechanics. Explore the different disturbing levels with your friends, while trying to escape from many puzzling entities.", "supported_languages": "English<strong>*</strong>, Spanish - Spain, Spanish - Latin America, French, German, Russian, Simplified Chinese<br><strong>*</strong>languages with full audio support", "header_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2419010/c8eb58848c3ea7e524eb44eef255f2a0763c91ac/header.jpg?t=1776161729", "capsule_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2419010/4b8ca38d293cf7bb931a6eda5d1b886ed196db95/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1776161729", "capsule_imagev5": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2419010/4b8ca38d293cf7bb931a6eda5d1b886ed196db95/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1776161729", "website": null, "pc_requirements": {"minimum": "<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system<br></li><li><strong>OS:</strong> Windows 10<br></li><li><strong>Processor:</strong> i3-8100 or equivalent<br></li><li><strong>Memory:</strong> 6 GB RAM<br></li><li><strong>Graphics:</strong> GTX 1050 or equivalent<br></li><li><strong>DirectX:</strong> Version 11<br></li><li><strong>Storage:</strong> 6 GB available space<br></li><li><strong>Sound Card:</strong> DirectX Compatible</li></ul>", "recommended": "<strong>Recommended:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system<br></li><li><strong>OS:</strong> Windows 11<br></li><li><strong>Processor:</strong> i5-10400 or equivalent<br></li><li><strong>Memory:</strong> 10 GB RAM<br></li><li><strong>Graphics:</strong> RTX 2060 or more<br></li><li><strong>DirectX:</strong> Version 12<br></li><li><strong>Network:</strong> Broadband Internet connection<br></li><li><strong>Storage:</strong> 6 GB available space<br></li><li><strong>Sound Card:</strong> DirectX Compatible</li></ul>"}, "mac_requirements": {"minimum": "<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"></ul>", "recommended": 